// An `i` directly after the digits of a decimal literal is the suffix, with a
// fractional part or without one (spec/01-lexical.md, rows `fractional-suffix`
// and `suffix-boundary`). Before the suffix existed, `1.5in [1.5]` was
// `1.5 in [1.5]`, a valid program that printed `true`. Now it is the literal
// `1.5i`, a fractional literal with the suffix, and the name `n`: a static
// error. A consumer that has no Int literal yet runs the program, so this
// probe fails today on every consumer and is on each expected-failure list.
//
// A static error rejects the program: a non-zero exit status, and nothing
// runs, so nothing prints (spec/README.md, Conformance). The first line
// prints `ran`, so an implementation that finds the error only when it runs
// the program prints `ran` and fails this probe.

print "ran";
print 1.5in [1.5];

// STATIC-ERROR
// STATUS: error
// COVERS: literal fractional-suffix
